## Color

Tokens live in `globals.css` as CSS custom properties. Never hardcode hex
values in components — reference the variable.

| Token              | Hex                      | Role                                                |
| ------------------ | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `--color-ink`       | `#171512`                | Primary text, nav background, footer                 |
| `--color-bone`      | `#FAFAF8` (v2, was `#F3EEE3`) | Page-level surface only (Hero, body) — see note below |
| `--color-white`     | `#FFFFFF`                | Card / product-tile surface — sits "above" the page   |
| `--color-moss`      | `#455A38`                | Primary accent — CTAs, active nav state, links        |
| `--color-clay`      | `#B5602E`                | Secondary accent — sale tags, highlights (sparingly)  |
| `--color-stone`     | `#8C8677`                | Muted text, dividers, secondary labels                |

**v2 note (white/product-forward direction):** the page background moved
from a warm bone tint to near-white, matching the product-photography-led
pattern used by major sportswear retailers. This introduced a **two-white
system**: `--color-bone` (`#FAFAF8`) is the page-level surface (Hero
section, `<body>`) and `--color-white` (`#FFFFFF`) is the elevated
surface for cards and product tiles. Depth between the two is carried by
`--shadow-card` / `--shadow-card-hover` and a hairline `border-stone/10`,
not by a background color difference alone — the two whites are close
enough that shadow/border are doing the real separation work.

**Rules:**
- Moss is the one accent allowed on primary CTAs. Never put moss and clay
  on the same CTA — clay is for badges/tags only, never buttons.
- Ink is a warm near-black, not pure `#000`. Never substitute `#000000`.
- Max one accent-filled button per view. Everything else is outline/ghost.
- Page-level surfaces (Hero, `<body>`) use `--color-bone`. Card/tile
  surfaces use `--color-white`. Don't use them interchangeably — that's
  what preserves the "lifted" feeling of product tiles.
- Form inputs (`input`, `textarea`, `select`) use a darker global border
  (`rgba(23, 21, 18, 0.25)`, ink-based) rather than the lighter
  `border-stone` tokens used on cards — inputs are interactive and need
  stronger boundary contrast (WCAG 1.4.11) than static containers do.
  Focus state uses `--color-moss`.

