## Known exceptions

These are intentional, tracked deviations from the token system —
documented so they read as decisions, not oversights, if a future
contributor (or Cline session) stumbles on them.

- **Auth pages** (`login`, `register`, `forgot-password`,
  `reset-password`) use a separate hex-based styling system
  (`border-[#1C1917]/20`, `bg-white`, `text-[#1C1917]`) rather than the
  `--color-ink` / `--color-white` tokens. `#1C1917` and `#171512` are two
  different near-black values from separate sources — visually close to
  indistinguishable, but not drawing from the same source of truth. This
  is a known gap, not a bug. **Next time auth pages are touched, migrate
  them onto the token system** rather than patching the hex values in
  place, so a future palette change doesn't silently miss these four
  pages.

